            <ArticleTitle>Intramuscular haemangioma of the thigh in a basketball player.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>346-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Haemangioma is a common benign soft tissue tumour. Intramuscular haemangiomas may present as a perceived sporting injury. Magnetic resonance imaging is the investigation of choice. Intramuscular haemangioma should be considered in the differential diagnosis of unexplained pain and swelling in a muscle.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
